## What Is Error Reporting?

FOSSBilling can send optional error reports to Sentry to help maintainers diagnose failures. See [Sentry's security practices](https://sentry.io/security/).

## What Gets Reported?

Reports can include error messages, stack traces, FOSSBilling and PHP versions, web server details, and your instance ID. FOSSBilling filters out expected errors such as validation failures.

FOSSBilling disables Sentry's default collection of personally identifiable information and strips the installation path from stack trace filenames. Reports can include incoming request URLs and query strings.

## Instance ID

In the admin sidebar, go to **System → Settings**, select **System**, and open the **About** tab. Share your instance ID when asking support to look up an error report.

## Enable or Disable Error Reporting

The installer asks whether to enable error reporting. After installation, use the **Error Reporting** tab in the **System** module or the [`report_errors` setting](/admin-guide/config/#debugging) in `config.php`.
